@page
@model WoodruffDev.Pages.Services.FractionalArchitectModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Fractional Architect";
}

<div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
        <span class="section-label">Service</span>
        <h1>Fractional Architect</h1>
        <p>Senior architecture leadership, embedded in your team&mdash;without the full-time hire.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="service-detail fade-in">
            <h2>Service Overview</h2>
            <p>Most growing engineering teams reach a point where the decisions in front of them are too consequential for the loudest voice in the room, but too specific for a generic consultant. A Fractional Architect fills that gap. I embed with your team for a set block of hours each week, sit in on the real conversations, own the architecture decisions that need an owner, and leave your engineers stronger than I found them.</p>
            <p>This isn&rsquo;t staff augmentation. It&rsquo;s senior technical leadership on a schedule that matches your stage, priced against outcomes&mdash;not a headcount line.</p>

            <h2>Signals You Need This</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>You&rsquo;ve grown past the point where one founding engineer can hold the whole system in their head</li>
                <li>Architecture decisions are being deferred, reversed, or re-litigated every sprint</li>
                <li>A cloud migration, rewrite, or platform unification is on the near horizon</li>
                <li>You&rsquo;ve just raised, just been acquired, or just lost a key technical leader</li>
                <li>A full-time principal or staff architect is the right role&mdash;but not the right spend yet</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>What You Get</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>4&ndash;16 hours per week of embedded architecture work, adjustable as needs shift</li>
                <li>Written architecture decision records (ADRs) the team can point to and push back on</li>
                <li>Design reviews, code reviews, and standing hours your engineers can book</li>
                <li>A documented reference architecture and a 90-day technical roadmap</li>
                <li>Hiring input: interview rubrics, candidate debriefs, leveling guidance</li>
                <li>Direct line to leadership with a plain-English translation layer</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>How It Works</h2>
            <h3>Step 1 &ndash; Discovery &amp; Alignment</h3>
            <p>A focused kickoff to map your goals, the constraints you&rsquo;re operating under, and the systems you already have. You leave the first week with a clear picture of what I&rsquo;ll be doing and what &ldquo;better&rdquo; looks like in 90 days.</p>
            <h3>Step 2 &ndash; Embedded Engagement</h3>
            <p>I join your standups, your design reviews, and the Slack channels that matter. I review PRs, write ADRs, and pair on the hardest calls. Typical cadence is 4&ndash;16 hours per week, scaled up during transitions and down when things stabilize.</p>
            <h3>Step 3 &ndash; Iteration &amp; Handoff</h3>
            <p>As your team matures, my involvement changes shape&mdash;deeper during migrations or hires, lighter during steady-state. When it&rsquo;s time for me to step back, your team has the artifacts and the confidence to run without me.</p>

            <h2>Troubleshooting Mode</h2>
            <p>When systems slow, teams stall, or architectural choices aren&rsquo;t aging well, I come in with a tighter scope:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Deep-dive technical assessments with written findings</li>
                <li>Root-cause analysis of architecture bottlenecks and failure modes</li>
                <li>Restructuring guidance with clear sequencing and trade-offs</li>
                <li>Direct, unvarnished recommendations&mdash;no filler, no hedging</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>Why Work With Me</h2>
            <p><strong>Decisions With Receipts</strong> &ndash; Every major call is written down with trade-offs, context, and a date. You shouldn&rsquo;t have to guess why choices were made.</p>
            <p><strong>Mentorship Built In</strong> &ndash; I don&rsquo;t just hand down architecture. I teach your engineers why it works, so the knowledge stays when I leave.</p>
            <p><strong>Business-to-Dev Translator</strong> &ndash; I make technical reality legible to leadership and strategic direction legible to engineers.</p>
            <p><strong>Flexible by Design</strong> &ndash; I adapt to your pace, team size, and current state. Chaos or calm&mdash;same rigor, different dial.</p>

            <div class="service-cta">
                <h3>Need an architect this quarter, not next fiscal year?</h3>
                <p>Let&rsquo;s talk about where your team is and what kind of engagement makes sense.</p>
                <a href="/Contact" class="btn btn-primary">Start the Conversation <span class="btn-arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
            </div>

            <div class="service-nav">
                <a href="/Services/Advisory">&larr; Advisory &amp; Board Roles</a>
                <a href="/Services/ExpertWitness">Expert Witness &rarr;</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
